   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualification to hold\nthe position of assistant district attorney in the county of Orange",
    "basePrintNo": "S8645",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8645-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8645\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public officers law, in relation to qualification to\nhold the position of assistant district attorney in the county of Orange\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nPermits residents of Orange county and adjoining counties to hold the\nposition of assistant district attorney in Orange county.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends public officers law by adding a new subdivision that\nauthorizes residents of counties which adjoin Orange County to serve as\nassistant district attorney in Orange County. This provision does not\napply to the position of chief assistant district attorney.\n\nSection 2: Sets effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill has been introduced at the request of the Orange County\nDistrict Attorney's Office. This legislation will allow Orange County to\nexpand its pool of eligible applicants and be able hire qualified indi-\nviduals from adjacent counties to hold the position of assistant\ndistrict attorney in Orange County. Similar authorizations have been\nprovided to multiple counties around NYS.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
